The Kerrville Folk Festival presents Quiet Valley Homecoming, October 23–25, 2026, at Quiet Valley Ranch, located at 3876 Medina Highway in Kerrville, Texas. This relaxed fall campout invites longtime festival fans, songwriters, and friends to return to the Hill Country for a weekend of community, connection, and the welcoming spirit that makes Kerrville special. Rather than a traditional music festival with a scheduled lineup, Homecoming encourages attendees to gather around campfires, share stories, join song circles, and enjoy informal, community-led activities.

While no formal performing artist lineup has been announced, attendees are encouraged to create their own musical experiences through campground song circles, hoot nights, storytelling sessions, art demonstrations, and shared meals. The weekend will also feature the Quiet Valley Ranch Chili Cookoff, with separate meat and vegetarian chili categories, adding a flavorful touch to the festivities. Weekend passes are $35 when purchased online or $40 at the gate, covering admission through noon on Monday, October 26. Quiet Valley Homecoming offers a wonderful opportunity to reconnect with the Kerrville Folk Festival family, celebrate the joy of songwriting, and enjoy an authentic Texas Hill Country gathering.

